WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:08.702
We taught OpenAI's Whisper to understand Finnish dialects: the speech of older people, and of much of Finland outside Helsinki.

00:10.102 --> 00:26.063
On interviews from ten municipalities the model never heard, it gets about one word in five wrong. Plain Whisper gets two in five, and paid services like Gemini, ElevenLabs and gpt-4o-transcribe do no better.

00:27.463 --> 00:36.371
On a second dialect corpus, three AI judges counted only the errors that change the meaning. Every judge puts our models far ahead.

00:37.771 --> 00:43.335
On read and parliament speech, it stays at Whisper's level. There, the commercial services lead.

00:44.735 --> 00:52.781
And for standard business Finnish, full of brand names, Gemini 3.5 Flash is the better pick. We measured that too.

00:54.181 --> 01:03.977
Almost ten hours of test audio, open data and an open model. Try it on Hugging Face, and find the code and every result on GitHub.
